=== the authority, booted alone: it makes its key and publishes the public half ===
time_clockbox: image built (16 expected lines)
enrolled: the authority's key, as the line it printed on its own console
=== the roll: the authority enrolled, the till not yet (it has not made its key) ===
roll: fleet nuage -- 2 members on lan, served by nobody in this fleet -- judged, no refusal
roll:   time -- the word of clockbox, and of nobody else, is what dates this fleet's records
roll:   clockbox -- time_clockbox (time_clockbox.machine, 10.30.0.1/24) -- 52:54:00:12:36:01 -- enrolled, fingerprint FP1
roll:   till -- time_till (time_till.machine, 10.30.0.2/24) -- 52:54:00:12:36:02 -- KEEPS A RECORD AND IS NOT ENROLLED: nobody can verify what it signs
roll: fleet nuage -- 1 member keeps a signed record that no holder of this file can check; enrol from the line the device prints on its own console
=== the till's image (built, not booted) ===
time_till: image built (17 expected lines)
=== round 1: declared -- the authority on the wire, the till booted three times on one disk ===
=== the roll: both enrolled ===
roll: fleet nuage -- 2 members on lan, served by nobody in this fleet -- judged, no refusal
roll:   time -- the word of clockbox, and of nobody else, is what dates this fleet's records
roll:   clockbox -- time_clockbox (time_clockbox.machine, 10.30.0.1/24) -- 52:54:00:12:36:01 -- enrolled, fingerprint FP1
roll:   till -- time_till (time_till.machine, 10.30.0.2/24) -- 52:54:00:12:36:02 -- enrolled, fingerprint FP2
=== round 2: alone -- nobody on the wire, the till booted twice more ===
=== round 3: an impostor -- a different machine answers from the authority's address ===
=== the till's disk, read back from the disk itself ===
disk: /data/journal.time holds 3 statements, byte for byte the ones the till published before the impostor answered, and none of the impostor's
disk: /data/journal holds 6 entries, one for each of the 6 boots
=== round 4: a statement the power cut short, on the till's disk -- and a boot it must not hold back ===
=== round 5: an authority whose clock will not answer, and one with no link to answer on ===
=== the clock the statements read ===
clock: 3 statements (the ones the till kept), the first no earlier than the emulator's clock base, each later than the one before, all within half an hour of the base: yes
=== the host: the record's entries, dated, by somebody who holds only the fleet file ===
dated: time: fleet nuage takes the time from clockbox, enrolled as fingerprint FP1
dated: time: the record has 2 entries, each shaped like one, hashing to what it says and chained to the one before it
dated: time: statement 1 verifies -- the entry H8 existed no later than <time>
dated: time:   that is entry 1 of 2: it, and every entry before it, existed no later than then
dated: time: statement 2 verifies -- the entry H8 existed no later than <time>
dated: time:   that is entry 2 of 2: it, and every entry before it, existed no later than then
dated: time: entry 1 existed no later than <time> (statement 1)
dated: time: entry 2 existed no later than <time> (statement 2)
dated: time: 2 statements verified against the key clockbox holds in this fleet, and no secret took part
dated: exit 0
=== ... and whose they are, by the same file and the other key ===
whose: fleet nuage -- till: 2 entries verified against the enrolled key (fingerprint FP2), and no secret took part
whose: fleet nuage -- till: its head is entry 2, hash=H -- the entry a RETIREMENT of this key would be trusted THROUGH
whose: exit 0
=== the host: after the authority went away -- what it said stays said, and what came after is undated ===
mixed: time: fleet nuage takes the time from clockbox, enrolled as fingerprint FP1
mixed: time: the record has 4 entries, each shaped like one, hashing to what it says and chained to the one before it
mixed: time: statement 1 verifies -- the entry H8 existed no later than <time>
mixed: time:   that is entry 1 of 4: it, and every entry before it, existed no later than then
mixed: time: statement 2 verifies -- the entry H8 existed no later than <time>
mixed: time:   that is entry 2 of 4: it, and every entry before it, existed no later than then
mixed: time: statement 3 verifies -- the entry H8 existed no later than <time>
mixed: time:   that is entry 3 of 4: it, and every entry before it, existed no later than then
mixed: time: entry 1 existed no later than <time> (statement 1)
mixed: time: entry 2 existed no later than <time> (statement 2)
mixed: time: entry 3 existed no later than <time> (statement 3)
mixed: time: entry 4 is ORDERED and UNDATED: no statement is about it, or about any entry after it
mixed: time: 3 statements verified against the key clockbox holds in this fleet, and no secret took part
mixed: exit 0
=== negative 1: one second added to a statement ===
changed: time: fleet nuage takes the time from clockbox, enrolled as fingerprint FP1
changed: time: the record has 4 entries, each shaped like one, hashing to what it says and chained to the one before it
changed: time: statement 1 does not verify: it was changed after it was signed, or signed by another key
changed: time: statement 2 verifies -- the entry H8 existed no later than <time>
changed: time:   that is entry 2 of 4: it, and every entry before it, existed no later than then
changed: time: statement 3 verifies -- the entry H8 existed no later than <time>
changed: time:   that is entry 3 of 4: it, and every entry before it, existed no later than then
changed: time: entry 1 existed no later than <time> (statement 2)
changed: time: entry 2 existed no later than <time> (statement 2)
changed: time: entry 3 existed no later than <time> (statement 3)
changed: time: entry 4 is ORDERED and UNDATED: no statement is about it, or about any entry after it
changed: time: 1 of 3 statements refused: what a refused statement says is not taken
changed: exit 1
=== negative 2: the same statements, offered to a fleet that takes its time from another machine ===
foreign: time: fleet nuage takes the time from clockbox, enrolled as fingerprint FP3
foreign: time: the record has 4 entries, each shaped like one, hashing to what it says and chained to the one before it
foreign: time: statement 1 was signed by somebody else than the time authority
foreign: time: statement 2 was signed by somebody else than the time authority
foreign: time: statement 3 was signed by somebody else than the time authority
foreign: time: entry 1 is ORDERED and UNDATED: no statement is about it, or about any entry after it
foreign: time: entry 2 is ORDERED and UNDATED: no statement is about it, or about any entry after it
foreign: time: entry 3 is ORDERED and UNDATED: no statement is about it, or about any entry after it
foreign: time: entry 4 is ORDERED and UNDATED: no statement is about it, or about any entry after it
foreign: time: 3 of 3 statements refused: what a refused statement says is not taken
foreign: exit 1
=== negative 3: an entry taken out of the record ===
removed: time: fleet nuage takes the time from clockbox, enrolled as fingerprint FP1
removed: time: record entry 3 is not the entry this place holds (seq=<its place> prev=...): an entry was removed, reordered or replaced, or this line is not an entry at all
removed: exit 1
=== negative 4: the record cut at its end, which still hashes and chains ===
cut: time: fleet nuage takes the time from clockbox, enrolled as fingerprint FP1
cut: time: the record has 2 entries, each shaped like one, hashing to what it says and chained to the one before it
cut: time: statement 1 verifies -- the entry H8 existed no later than <time>
cut: time:   that is entry 1 of 2: it, and every entry before it, existed no later than then
cut: time: statement 2 verifies -- the entry H8 existed no later than <time>
cut: time:   that is entry 2 of 2: it, and every entry before it, existed no later than then
cut: time: statement 3 verifies -- the entry H8 existed no later than <time>
cut: time: statement 3 is about an entry this record does not hold: it is another record's, or entries were cut from the end of this one
cut: time: entry 1 existed no later than <time> (statement 1)
cut: time: entry 2 existed no later than <time> (statement 2)
cut: time: 1 of 3 statements refused: what a refused statement says is not taken
cut: exit 1
=== negative 5: nothing to verify ===
nothing: time: fleet nuage takes the time from clockbox, enrolled as fingerprint FP1
nothing: time: the record has 4 entries, each shaped like one, hashing to what it says and chained to the one before it
nothing: time: no statement is kept: every entry of this record is ORDERED and UNDATED
nothing: time: a verification of nothing is not one: the file holds no statement
nothing: exit 1
=== negative 6: a fleet that takes its time from nobody ===
nobody: time: fleet salle_makeen declares no time authority: there is no key a statement could be checked against, so none is taken
nobody: exit 1
=== what each machine said ===
enrol: the machine with the clock, booted on a disk that has never held its key:
enrol: boot: harb init -- machine time_clockbox (hosted / x86_64 / qemu_pc) -- pid 1
enrol: boot: console /dev/ttyS0
enrol: boot: mount proc at /proc -- done
enrol: boot: mount sysfs at /sys -- done
enrol: boot: mount devtmpfs at /dev -- done
enrol: boot: mount ext4 at /data -- done
enrol: boot: grant process (effectful)
enrol: boot: grant filesystem (effectful)
enrol: boot: grant network (effectful)
enrol: boot: network lan -- eth0 up 10.30.0.1/24
enrol: boot: identity -- ed25519, custody a file at /data/device.key -- created on this device, fingerprint FP1
enrol: boot: time -- lan answers on 10.30.0.1:7000: an entry it is asked about, signed with this device's key and the time /dev/rtc0 reads; the floor keeps no time of its own
enrol: boot: confine -- attest has no network of its own; what a world did not declare, the kernel does not give it
enrol: boot: floor -- the machine is not a world's to change: none may mount or unmount, set the clock, load a module, rename the host, make or enter a namespace, trace another process, or reboot the box
enrol: boot: start attest -- pid N -- /harb attest --export
enrol: attest time_clockbox -- ed25519, fingerprint FP1
enrol: enrol time_clockbox ed25519 KEY1 -- KEY for this machine's MEMBER in a fleet
enrol: attest: signed 21 bytes with this device's key and verified them against its public half
enrol: attest: one bit flipped in the message, and the same signature is refused
enrol: boot: attest (pid N) exited 0
enrol: boot: judge -- the boot matches its expectation (/etc/expected, 16 lines)
enrol: boot: every service has ended -- and this machine is still the time authority of lan: a server stops when the machine stops, not when the asking does
